\fill (0.7,2.9) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above right] at (0.7,2.9) {$A$};
\fill (3.7,0.7) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above right] at (3.7,0.7) {$B$};
\node at (3.2,2.6) {$m < 0$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A horizontal interval has $y_2 = y_1$, so the rise is $0$ and the gradient is $0$.

[tikz]
